    {
        "content": "<p>this works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PowerSeries</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WithPiTopology</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PowerSeries</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PowerSeries</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HasProd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PowerSeries</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PowerSeries</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HasProd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">convert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">postTransparency</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">implicit</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- eliminated the typeclass goal</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ⊢ c = a R</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ⊢ d = b R</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 617589248,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1787194343
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>maybe <code>convert</code> should bump its transparency in the same way that <code>isDefEq</code> does?</p>",
        "id": 617589264,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1787194360
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh it looks like this is from <code>convert</code> calling <code>congr!</code>, maybe <code>congr!</code> should bump its transparency then</p>",
        "id": 617589371,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1787194435
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>After the transparency update, the <code>convert</code> and <code>congr</code> will produce such things provable by <code>rfl</code>. Which breaks some of my old code. My solution is use <code>convert!</code> and <code>congr!</code> with explicit level to prevent it unfolds too much.</p>",
        "id": 617607067,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1787205419
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there something about <code>MvPowerSeries.instCommRing.toCommMonoid</code> and <code>MvPowerSeries.instCommSemiring.toCommMonoid</code> that should be fixed?</p>",
        "id": 617809090,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1787269439
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40663\">#40663</a> will make <code>convert</code> solve goals at instance transparency. For now, you can also write: <code>convert (preTransparency := instances) foo R</code>.</p>",
        "id": 617937113,
        "sender_full_name": "Anne Baanen",
        "timestamp": 1787320784
    }
]